Stop reading an ascii-format serialized string at end of input.

InString() reads each character of an ascii-format string with
GetChar(), which for a FILE stream is fgetc() and for a text connection
is Rconn_fgetc(). Both return EOF without an error, so a declared string
length larger than the rest of the input filled the remaining bytes with
0xff and carried on. With a 2 GB declared length the invalid-UTF-8
warning path then re-encoded 2 GB of 0xff bytes one iconv() call per
byte. Error out at EOF instead, as the binary and xdr readers already do.

A standalone reproducer is:
    x <- strrep("a", 100)
    s <- rawToChar(serialize(x, NULL, ascii = TRUE))
    tc <- textConnection(substr(s, 1, nchar(s) - 50))
    unserialize(tc)   # returned "aaa...\n\xff\xff..." rather than an error

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R), not
carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 5785070217265152 (libFuzzer_r_load, Timeout
in reEnc4 / invalid_utf8_warning / ReadChar).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #396, filed 2026-10-21.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

--- a/src/main/serialize.c
+++ b/src/main/serialize.c
@@ -514,8 +514,15 @@
 		;
 	    UngetChar(&iss, c);
 	    for (i = 0; i < length; i++) {
-		if ((c =  GetChar(&iss)) == '\\') {
-		    switch(c = GetChar(&iss)) {
+		/* fgetc() and text connections return EOF without an
+		   error: stop here rather than fill the rest of the
+		   string with EOF bytes */
+		if ((c = GetChar(&iss)) == EOF)
+		    error(_("read error"));
+		if (c == '\\') {
+		    if ((c = GetChar(&iss)) == EOF)
+			error(_("read error"));
+		    switch(c) {
 		    case 'n' : buf[i] = '\n'; break;
 		    case 't' : buf[i] = '\t'; break;
 		    case 'v' : buf[i] = '\v'; break;
